Now the rain stops.
In the evening, a cool wind blows.
I stand at the bus stop.
That bus arrives.
I board the bus.
The conductor comes.
I buy a ticket from the conductor.
I sit near the window.
These streets are wet.
They shine with the water.
I look outside, and I think.
Five months ago, I boarded a bus here for the first time.
Then, I was very nervous.
That experience was completely new.
Now this bus is familiar to me.
That time was different, this time is different.
This city is now like my home.
The bus goes, and I smile peacefully.
